lican consolidation could narrow the margin, though nothing in current evidence suggests that is underway.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's governor race pits first-term incumbent Josh Shapiro against Republican State Treasurer Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Shapiro enters the fall with overwhelming advantages: polls since June consistently show him ahead by double digits, including a Siena survey of likely voters at 55 to 39 in late August. Every major race rating, from Cook to Sabato, places the contest in Safe or Solid Democratic territory.\n\nThe resource gap is stark. Shapiro has raised roughly $60 million and outspends Garrity about 20 to 1, including $2.4 million on ads in a single week against $672 from his opponent. Prediction markets put his win chances at 96 to 97 percent. Garrity is campaigning statewide, but the fundamentals and money leave her with little visible path to closing the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 17.5}]}